subtitle: What did we expect?

Expectedly, the <span style="color: #C0A054;">**DVP**</span> has resoundingly rejected the proposed school bill, viewing it as an affront to their ideals of the separation of church and state. With little room for compromise, we have therefore decided to collapse the Fourth Marx Cabinet. However, in accordance with Hindenburg’s wishes, the coalition will pass the budget for the upcoming year before the upcoming elections in May. 

Despite Marx IV achieving legislative successes in social policy, labor-management relations have deteriorated sharply, with class conflict flaring up within the party. Marx, who also serves as Chairman of the Catholic Schools Association, has faced considerable criticism from the rank and file over the failure of the school law. He has since announced that he will resign at the next party congress in December. 

With the formation of the <span style="color: #909090;">**CSRP**</span> and the growing appeal of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>, the outlook for the upcoming election in May looks increasingly bleak.

@accept
